// src/user/ime/indic_inscript.pdx -- G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322)
//
// INDIC IME PROVIDER SATELLITE (InScript + Phonetic).
//
// A userspace IME provider process that registers with the KIND_IME_
// PROVIDER substrate (§2.19, sibling landing #2315, LANDED B10) under
// LANG_INDIC_HI and services Hindi (Devanagari) input via two
// orthogonal typing disciplines united behind one engine cell:
//
//   * MODE_INSCRIPT (=0).  The Bureau of Indian Standards InScript
//     keymap (IS 13194:1991, refreshed 2002 and adopted by every
//     modern Indic OS distribution) is a direct-map keyboard layout:
//     each of the 128 primary + shifted keys on a US-QWERTY layout
//     produces exactly one Devanagari codepoint. The user types
//     `k` -> `क` (U+0915), `Shift+K` -> `ख` (U+0916), etc. No
//     preedit, no candidate window, no delay -- every keystroke
//     commits a single glyph via a table lookup on the keymap.
//     InScript is the canonical Indic typing method (taught in
//     Indian schools, prescribed by the Central government for
//     Devanagari input in official work) and this file's default
//     mode at init.
//
//   * MODE_PHONETIC (=1).  A Roman-alphabet-to-Devanagari
//     transliteration engine: the user types Roman letters
//     ("namaste"), the engine accumulates them into a prefix, and on
//     a word boundary (Space or Enter) resolves the prefix into a
//     Devanagari string ("नमस्ते") which is committed to the bound
//     session. This mode targets users who know the sounds but not
//     the InScript keymap (a large first-time-Devanagari-user
//     audience -- overseas Indians typing on non-Indic keyboards,
//     Hindi learners, second-language users). The resolution table
//     itself is out of scope for this landing (deferred to the
//     satellite-side substrate that wires the transliteration
//     dictionary, mirroring how latin_deadkey's compose-table
//     lookup is stubbed until its substrate lands). The state
//     machine that ACCUMULATES the Roman prefix and DISPATCHES to
//     the (stubbed) resolver is fully implemented here.
//
// Both modes register a SINGLE provider row with LANG_INDIC_HI;
// switching modes at runtime does NOT re-register (a re-register
// would bump the router-side registered_seq and shuffle the router's
// most-recent-wins ordering, which is not what the user asked for
// when they toggled a personal-preference bit). The caps bitmap
// advertised at registration covers BOTH modes' capability sets:
// IMP_CAP_PREEDIT | IMP_CAP_PHONETIC = 0x05 (phonetic mode uses
// preedit ghost text while accumulating; InScript direct mode uses
// neither, but advertising unused capabilities is legal per the
// caps-bitmap contract -- the router refuses only bits ABOVE
// IMP_CAP_ALL, not extra bits within the defined family).
//
// Design authority:
//   * design/compositor/pwp-spec-vocabulary.md §2.19 KIND_IME_PROVIDER
//     -- names Indic (Devanagari) + InScript as the sixth of the
//     seven canonical provider families (Latin, Pinyin, Zhuyin,
//     Kana, Hangul, Devanagari, InScript). This landing implements
//     the Indic Hindi provider; sibling Indic scripts (Tamil,
//     Bengali, Gujarati, ...) land in follow-up rows under the
//     LANG_INDIC_TA / LANG_INDIC_BN / ... enum slots.
//   * src/user/ime/provider_kind.pdx §1.3 (LANG_INDIC_HI = 4) --
//     the enum slot this file's registration uses.
//   * src/user/ime/session_kind.pdx §1.3 (COMMIT_TEXT op semantics)
//     -- the router-side commit path this file's on_key + commit
//     feeds when either a direct InScript keystroke commits or a
//     resolved phonetic prefix commits.
//   * Bureau of Indian Standards IS 13194:1991 (Indian Script Code
//     for Information Interchange, ISCII) + the InScript keymap
//     annex -- the canonical prior art for MODE_INSCRIPT. The 128-
//     entry keymap this file's on_key body probes is a caller-
//     provided pointer whose layout matches IS 13194's keycode ->
//     Devanagari codepoint mapping (US-QWERTY base + Shift plane).
//   * Precedents: latin_autocomplete.pdx (#2317, LANDED B11) for
//     the register-once + per-keystroke accumulator schema, and
//     latin_deadkey.pdx (#2318, LANDED B12) for the stateful state-
//     machine + stubbed lookup pattern.
//
// TWO-MODE SINGLE-PROVIDER RATIONALE (vs. Latin's two separate
// providers). Latin autocomplete (#2317) and Latin dead-key (#2318)
// register as TWO providers because their user-facing disciplines are
// orthogonal -- one predicts words from a prefix, the other composes
// diacritics from combining keys. A user typically wants BOTH active
// simultaneously (autocomplete for word completion, dead-key for é/à/ô).
// InScript vs. phonetic Devanagari are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE at typing
// time -- the SAME keystroke `n` means DIFFERENT things (in InScript
// it produces `म`; in phonetic it accumulates as the letter `n`
// waiting to be resolved). A single provider with a mode toggle is the
// cleaner model: only one is active at any given moment, and the
// router does not need to arbitrate between two providers claiming
// the same (lang, locale) slot for orthogonal reasons. The mode-
// switch primitive (inscript_switch_mode) flips the bit; the next
// on_key uses the new mode.
//
// SCHEMA-ONLY PHONETIC LOOKUP. The phonetic transliteration table is
// NOT passed in at init time -- MODE_PHONETIC's resolver is a stub
// that clears the prefix and returns 0 (no output) on space/enter.
// The real resolver lands with the satellite-side substrate that
// wires the transliteration dictionary (a trie or FST over Roman
// syllable strings with Devanagari codepoint-sequence leaves,
// out of scope for this row). The state machine's correctness does
// NOT depend on the resolver body: an accumulating prefix, a
// word-boundary trigger, and a clear-on-resolve are all exercisable
// against the stub. MODE_INSCRIPT's keymap IS provided at init time
// (keymap_ptr) but its layout is likewise caller-defined; this file
// treats the pointer as opaque and probes it via a single u8-indexed
// dereference (the 128-entry table is a flat array of u16 codepoints,
// zero-filled for unmapped slots).
//
// PER-PROCESS SATELLITE. One engine per satellite process (a typical
// paideia-os machine runs one Hindi IME satellite; a multi-lingual
// user might run one per Indic script). The engine cell is CALLER-
// OWNED (mirrors focus_router / latin_autocomplete / latin_deadkey
// precedent); this file does not hold a module singleton. Multiple
// engines per process is legal (a user with two different InScript
// keymap variants) but unusual.
//
// INDIC INSCRIPT ENGINE STRUCT. The natural typing is
//
//   struct InScriptEngine {
//     provider_kind_id: u32,          // row_id from ime_provider_register
//     mode: u8,                        // MODE_INSCRIPT / MODE_PHONETIC
//     session_kind_id: u32,            // currently-bound session (0 = not bound)
//     keymap_ptr: u64,                 // pointer to 128-entry keycode -> codepoint
//     phonetic_prefix_offset: u32,     // interned Roman prefix; 0 = empty
//     pending_output_offset: u32,      // interned resolved Devanagari; 0 = none
//   }
//
// but paideia-as does not return structs by value from asm bodies
// (mirrors the note in latin_autocomplete.pdx / latin_deadkey.pdx /
// focus_router.pdx / input_server precedent), so the wire-level shape
// is a 32-byte caller-owned cell populated in place via fixed-offset
// word writes, and the init factory returns a u64 status code rather
// than the struct itself. Struct declaration is DOCUMENTATION ONLY.
//
// The prompt's `inscript_init(provider, mode, keymap_ptr) -> InScriptEngine`
// signature is reshaped to
//   inscript_init(engine_ptr, process_kind_id, mode, keymap_ptr) -> u64
// per the schema-parallel precedent above.
//
// LABEL PREFIX. `indic_inscript_` throughout, sidestepping paideia-as
// reserved-word collisions (see feedback_paideia_as_reserved_labels).
// Every ASM jump target is `indic_inscript_<funcname>_<tag>`.
//
// MECE SCOPE. Single file under src/user/ime/. Touches only:
//   * NEW: src/user/ime/indic_inscript.pdx (this file)
//   * EDIT: tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh (add allowlist entry
//           for pdx_kind_indic_inscript_meta since the satellite-side
//           dispatcher that would emit it is a future landing)
// No other file is modified.
//
// FAILURE BAND. 0xFFFFE7F0..0xFFFFE7FF -- the sixth of the seven
// G11.M4 provider bands, adjacent to the sibling LANG_LATIN provider
// bands (autocomplete 0xFFFFE7A0..AF, deadkey 0xFFFFE7B0..BF) with
// the intermediate 0xFFFFE7C0..EF pages reserved for the CJK/Indic
// siblings that land between them (Pinyin, Zhuyin, Kana, Hangul,
// Devanagari-standalone). Grep-verified free across src/ + tests/ +
// design/ at landing time (E7F is a fresh 16-slot page; the row
// prompt's naming survives the verification).
//
// FINGERPRINT. One legacy-suffixed init fingerprint per the standard
// klog convention (matches session_kind / provider_kind / latin_
// autocomplete / latin_deadkey precedent). Emitted once on successful
// engine init by the future satellite-side substrate; no fingerprint
// on the per-keystroke on_key / commit / switch_mode / reset paths
// (those fire many times per second and would flood the ring, same
// rationale as tag_tty_read_ok in keys.pdx). Until the substrate
// lands, the tag is DATA-ONLY (declared here but not emitted from
// any body) -- verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh gets a matching
// allowlist entry per the sibling B8 / B10 / B11 / B12 pattern.
//
// Encoder-conservative pattern per session_kind / provider_kind /
// latin_autocomplete / latin_deadkey: no `and reg, imm64`, no MOVABS
// r64,imm64, no `test`, no `add reg,[mem]`, no `mov_bzx`/`mov_wzx`;
// 32-bit zero-extension via shl+shr; small immediates only. u16 field
// extraction uses shl 48 / shr 48. u8 field extraction uses shl 56 /
// shr 56. Table-index reads use mov [ptr + rcx * 2] with the u16
// load reinterpreted via shl 48 / shr 48 (no mov_wzx).
//
// =============================================================================

module IndicInscript = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.1 -- PROVIDER-FAMILY PINS (mirror of ProviderKind)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Named locally so assembly bodies can use small immediates rather
  // than cross-module symbol references. Each pin is asserted in a
  // comment against its source of truth so a future edit to the
  // sibling module cannot silently drift.

  // Mirror of ProviderKind.LANG_INDIC_HI (= 4). Hindi (Devanagari)
  // slot. Sibling Indic scripts (Tamil = 5) will register under
  // their own LANG_INDIC_* slot in follow-up landings; this file
  // hard-codes the Hindi slot because InScript's keymap IS Hindi-
  // Devanagari-specific (Tamil InScript is a distinct 128-entry
  // table, and the phonetic transliteration dictionary is likewise
  // per-script).
  pub let IIS_LANG_INDIC_HI            : u64 = 4

  // Mirror of ProviderKind.IME_PROVIDER_LOCALE_UNLOCALED (= 0).
  // Hindi Devanagari input is not locale-partitioned within the
  // Devanagari family (hi-IN, mr-IN, ne-NP all use the same
  // InScript keymap and the same phonetic transliteration for the
  // shared code point range). Devanagari-with-Indian-locale vs.
  // Devanagari-with-Nepali-locale is a font/collation concern the
  // shaping layer handles, not the input method.
  pub let IIS_LOCALE_UNLOCALED         : u64 = 0

  // Mirror of ProviderKind.IMP_CAP_PREEDIT (0x01) | IMP_CAP_
  // PHONETIC (0x04) = 0x05. Advertises capabilities that cover
  // BOTH modes: MODE_PHONETIC uses preedit ghost text while
  // accumulating the Roman prefix; MODE_INSCRIPT uses neither (it
  // commits per-keystroke, no preedit visible). Advertising unused
  // bits is legal (provider_kind's IMP_BAD_CAPS validator refuses
  // ONLY bits ABOVE IMP_CAP_ALL = 0x0F, not extra bits within the
  // defined family). Not advertised: IMP_CAP_CANDIDATE_WINDOW
  // (0x02) -- neither mode draws a candidate list, so the router
  // will not offer this provider to a session that explicitly
  // requests candidate-window semantics.
  pub let IIS_CAPS_DEFAULT             : u64 = 0x05

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.2 -- ENGINE CELL LAYOUT (InScriptEngine, 32 bytes)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Four u64 words holding the engine's per-instance state. Every
  // mutating op edits one packed field IN PLACE; the row is written
  // by exactly one thread at a time (the satellite process's own
  // event loop is single-threaded per engine instance, mirroring the
  // per-seat single-thread invariant of focus_router / the per-
  // engine single-thread invariant of latin_autocomplete /
  // latin_deadkey).
  //
  // Cell layout (offsets in bytes):
  //
  //   [+0]  provider_and_session:
  //             provider_kind_id[31:0]   row_id from ime_provider_
  //                                      register at init time. Non-
  //                                      zero after successful init;
  //                                      0 before init.
  //             session_kind_id[63:32]   currently-bound session
  //                                      (router-updated via bind/
  //                                      unbind, out of scope for
  //                                      THIS landing). 0 = not
  //                                      bound (the engine still
  //                                      processes keys and updates
  //                                      state, but a completed
  //                                      commit emits no COMMIT_TEXT
  //                                      event because no session is
  //                                      listening).
  //
  //   [+8]  keymap_ptr: u64
  //             pointer to the 128-entry InScript keycode -> code
  //             point table. Each entry is a u16 Devanagari code
  //             point (or 0 for an unmapped slot). Table lives in
  //             the satellite process's own .data or in a shared
  //             read-only mapping. Nonzero after successful init.
  //             Layout is caller-defined; the on_key body treats
  //             it as a flat u16[128] array indexed by the low 7
  //             bits of the keycode.
  //
  //             KEYMAP TAIL-PADDING REQUIREMENT. Because paideia-as
  //             forbids mov_wzx (u16 zero-extended load), the on_key
  //             body reads the u16 slot via a 64-bit load followed
  //             by shl 48 / shr 48. That 64-bit load can read up to
  //             6 bytes past the last u16 slot (keycode 127 reads
  //             bytes 254..261). Callers MUST allocate the keymap
  //             with at least 8 bytes of tail padding (allocation
  //             size >= 264 bytes) so the tail read lands on the
  //             caller's own memory. A page-aligned allocation
  //             satisfies this trivially (a page is 4096 bytes).
  //             The satellite process's own keymap provisioner is
  //             responsible for enforcing this; the substrate has
  //             no in-band way to check it.
  //
  //   [+16] mode_and_prefix:
  //             mode[7:0]                     MODE_INSCRIPT(0) /
  //                                           MODE_PHONETIC(1)
  //             reserved[31:8]                0 at init; future
  //                                           mode extensions
  //                                           (Vedic Sanskrit
  //                                           annotation mode, etc)
  //             phonetic_prefix_offset[63:32] interned string offset
  //                                           into the satellite-
  //                                           side preedit pool.
  //                                           Meaningful only in
  //                                           MODE_PHONETIC; 0 =
  //                                           empty prefix (no
  //                                           accumulation in
  //                                           flight). Kept as 0
  //                                           throughout in MODE_
  //                                           INSCRIPT.
  //
  //   [+24] pending_and_reserved:
  //             pending_output_offset[31:0]   interned string offset
  //                                           of the resolved
  //                                           Devanagari output
  //                                           waiting for
  //                                           inscript_commit to
  //                                           dispatch to the
  //                                           session. Set by the
  //                                           phonetic-resolve arm
  //                                           of on_key; cleared by
  //                                           inscript_commit and
  //                                           inscript_reset. 0 =
  //                                           no pending output.
  //             reserved[63:32]               0 at init; future
  //                                           flags (input-mode
  //                                           hints, script-variant
  //                                           selectors) land here.
  //
  // Cell is 32 bytes = one half of a 64-byte cache line. Cache-line
  // alignment is CALLER'S responsibility (mirrors sibling latin_
  // deadkey).
  //
  // Documentation-only struct declaration (mirrors FocusRouterState /
  // LatinAutocompleteEngine / DeadkeyEngine precedent).

  struct InScriptEngine {
    provider_kind_id: u32,
    mode: u8,
    session_kind_id: u32,
    keymap_ptr: u64,
    phonetic_prefix_offset: u32,
    pending_output_offset: u32
  }

  pub let IIS_CELL_BYTES                : u64 = 32
  pub let IIS_CELL_OFF_PROVIDER_SESSION : u64 = 0
  pub let IIS_CELL_OFF_KEYMAP_PTR       : u64 = 8
  pub let IIS_CELL_OFF_MODE_PREFIX      : u64 = 16
  pub let IIS_CELL_OFF_PENDING          : u64 = 24

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.3 -- InScriptMode ENUM
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Two mutually exclusive typing disciplines the engine supports.
  // The mode is set at init time and toggled at runtime via
  // inscript_switch_mode.

  pub let IIS_MODE_INSCRIPT        : u64 = 0
  pub let IIS_MODE_PHONETIC        : u64 = 1
  pub let IIS_MODE_MAX             : u64 = 1  // inclusive upper bound

  // Keymap dimensions. 128 entries covers the US-QWERTY base +
  // Shift plane the InScript layout occupies. Wider keymaps (US
  // international, extended AltGr planes) are handled by successive
  // keymap_ptr swaps rather than a wider fixed size, keeping this
  // file's range gate a small immediate.
  pub let IIS_KEYMAP_SIZE          : u64 = 128

  // Word-boundary sentinels that trigger phonetic resolution in
  // MODE_PHONETIC. When the accumulator sees one of these keycodes,
  // it invokes the resolver on the accumulated prefix, commits the
  // resolved output, and clears the prefix.
  pub let IIS_KEYSYM_SPACE         : u64 = 0x0020
  pub let IIS_KEYSYM_ENTER         : u64 = 0x000D
  pub let IIS_KEYSYM_ESC           : u64 = 0x001B  // reset trigger

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.4 -- FAILURE TAXONOMY (0xFFFFE7F0..0xFFFFE7FF)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Fresh 16-wide band. Row prompt names 0xFFFFE7F0..FF; grep-
  // verified free across src/ + tests/ + design/ at landing time.
  // Sixth of the seven G11.M4 provider bands (adjacent to the
  // Latin bands at 0xFFFFE7A0..AF and 0xFFFFE7B0..BF).

  pub let IIS_OK                   : u64 = 0
  pub let IIS_ENGINE_NULL          : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FF  // engine_ptr == 0
  pub let IIS_PROCESS_NULL         : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FE  // process_kind_id == 0
  pub let IIS_KEYMAP_NULL          : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FD  // keymap_ptr == 0
  pub let IIS_BAD_MODE             : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FC  // mode > IIS_MODE_MAX
  pub let IIS_ALREADY_INIT         : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FB  // engine already initialized
  pub let IIS_NOT_INIT             : u64 = 0xFFFFE7FA  // op before init succeeded
  pub let IIS_REGISTER_REFUSED     : u64 = 0xFFFFE7F9  // ime_provider_register
                                                        // returned refusal sentinel
                                                        // (upper 32 bits set)
  pub let IIS_BAD_KEYCODE          : u64 = 0xFFFFE7F8  // keycode >= IIS_KEYMAP_SIZE
  pub let IIS_BAD_STATE            : u64 = 0xFFFFE7F7  // cell mode field > MODE_MAX
                                                        // (corruption detection;
                                                        // defence-in-depth against
                                                        // a rogue writer to
                                                        // cell[+16][7:0])
  pub let IIS_NO_PENDING           : u64 = 0xFFFFE7F6  // commit with no pending
                                                        // output
  // Slots 0xFFFFE7F5..0xFFFFE7F0 are RESERVED within this file's
  // band for future extension (keymap-checksum failures, resolver-
  // dictionary integrity failures once the substrate lands).

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.5 -- ON-KEY RETURN-CODE TAGS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The on_key body returns a u64 whose upper 32 bits are ZERO on
  // success (distinguishable from refusals, whose upper 32 bits are
  // set per the sibling latin_deadkey convention). The success
  // encoding packs a small tag in the low byte and, for the
  // COMMITTED path, the composed u16 code point in bits [23:8]:
  //
  //   bits [7:0]     tag (IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH / IIS_TAG_PENDING /
  //                  IIS_TAG_COMMITTED / IIS_TAG_RESOLVED)
  //   bits [23:8]    u16 code point; meaningful only when tag ==
  //                  IIS_TAG_COMMITTED (InScript direct commit),
  //                  zero otherwise
  //   bits [63:24]   0
  //
  // Callers demux via the low byte. For IIS_TAG_RESOLVED (phonetic
  // resolution complete), the caller reads pending_output_offset
  // via inscript_get_pending or invokes inscript_commit to dispatch
  // the resolved string.

  pub let IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH      : u64 = 0
  pub let IIS_TAG_PENDING          : u64 = 1  // phonetic accumulating
  pub let IIS_TAG_COMMITTED        : u64 = 2  // InScript direct: u16 in [23:8]
  pub let IIS_TAG_RESOLVED         : u64 = 3  // phonetic resolved; read
                                              // pending_output_offset

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.6 -- FINGERPRINT (one line, legacy-suffixed)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // pdx_kind_indic_inscript_meta: emitted once on successful engine
  // init by the future satellite-side substrate. Data-only at this
  // landing per the sibling B8 / B10 / B11 / B12 pattern
  // (allowlisted in tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh as "indic
  // inscript init ok [legacy: INDIC INSCRIPT INIT OK]").
  //
  // Byte count: 55 content chars + 1 NUL = 56.
  pub let pdx_kind_indic_inscript_meta : [u8; 56] = "indic inscript init ok [legacy: INDIC INSCRIPT INIT OK]\0"

  // Short field-name string constants for future debug-print use
  // (mirror ime_provider_k_row_id / latin_deadkey_k_provider_id
  // precedent).
  pub let indic_inscript_k_provider_id : [u8; 12] = "provider_id\0"
  pub let indic_inscript_k_mode        : [u8; 5]  = "mode\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- STATS CELL
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Module-level counters shared across every engine instance in
  // this process (typically one). Mirrors _latin_deadkey_stats /
  // _latin_autocomplete_stats / _provider_kind_stats layout.

  pub let mut _indic_inscript_stats : [u64; 8] = uninit @align(64)

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- STATS COUNTER SLOTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Eight named slots. A boot-log observer can verify KEY_EVENTS >=
  // COMMITS + RESOLVES + RESETS (each commit, each resolve, and each
  // explicit reset consumes at least one prior key event).

  pub let IIS_ST_KEY_EVENTS        : u64 = 0
  pub let IIS_ST_COMMITS           : u64 = 1  // InScript direct commit or
                                              // inscript_commit dispatch of
                                              // resolved phonetic output
  pub let IIS_ST_ACCUMULATES       : u64 = 2  // phonetic prefix extended
  pub let IIS_ST_RESOLVES          : u64 = 3  // phonetic prefix resolved
                                              // (space/enter fired the resolver)
  pub let IIS_ST_RESETS            : u64 = 4  // ESC or explicit reset
  pub let IIS_ST_MODE_SWITCHES     : u64 = 5
  pub let IIS_ST_INITS             : u64 = 6
  pub let IIS_ST_REFUSED           : u64 = 7
  pub let IIS_ST_MAX               : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 4 -- COUNTER PRIMITIVES
  // ==========================================================================

  // indic_inscript_stats_reset() -> (): zero counters at boot.
  pub let indic_inscript_stats_reset : () -> () !{mem} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): clear per-module counters at boot. Mirrors latin_deadkey_stats_reset. Single low-first index scan over 8 u64 slots via load-inc-store; no callee-save pushes (leaf; only r10/rcx/rax touched beyond SysV in/out). Labels prefixed indic_inscript_srs_.",
      block: {
        lea r10, [rip + _indic_inscript_stats];
        xor rax, rax;
        xor rcx, rcx;
      indic_inscript_srs_loop:
        mov [r10 + rcx * 8], rax;
        add rcx, 1;
        cmp rcx, 8;
        jb  indic_inscript_srs_loop;
        ret
      }
    }

  // indic_inscript_note(which) -> (): bump one stats counter.
  // Encoder-conservative load-inc-store; OOB is a silent no-op.
  pub let indic_inscript_note : (u64) -> () !{mem} @{} =
    fn (which: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): counter bump. Encoder-conservative load-inc-store; no add reg,[mem]. OOB is a silent no-op. Mirrors latin_deadkey_note. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_nt_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        jae indic_inscript_nt_out;
        lea r10, [rip + _indic_inscript_stats];
        mov rax, [r10 + rdi * 8];
        add rax, 1;
        mov [r10 + rdi * 8], rax;
      indic_inscript_nt_out:
        ret
      }
    }

  // indic_inscript_stat(which) -> u64: read one stats counter.
  pub let indic_inscript_stat : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (which: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): counter read; OOB -> 0. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_st_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        jae indic_inscript_st_zero;
        lea r10, [rip + _indic_inscript_stats];
        mov rax, [r10 + rdi * 8];
        ret;
      indic_inscript_st_zero:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 5 -- VALIDATORS (pure leaves)
  // ==========================================================================

  // indic_inscript_mode_valid(mode) -> 1 iff mode <= IIS_MODE_MAX.
  pub let indic_inscript_mode_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (mode: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): 1 iff mode in {0,1}. Small-immediate cmp; encoder-conservative. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_mv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 1;
        ja  indic_inscript_mv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      indic_inscript_mv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // indic_inscript_keycode_valid(keycode) -> 1 iff keycode <
  // IIS_KEYMAP_SIZE (128). Keymap is a flat u16[128] array; a
  // keycode outside that range cannot index the table and is
  // refused with IIS_BAD_KEYCODE.
  pub let indic_inscript_keycode_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (keycode: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): 1 iff keycode < 128. Small-immediate cmp; encoder-conservative. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_kv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 128;
        jae indic_inscript_kv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      indic_inscript_kv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 6 -- CELL-FIELD GETTERS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every getter takes the engine_ptr in rdi and returns the
  // requested field in rax. A null engine_ptr is undefined behavior
  // at the getter level (mirrors focus_router_get_* / input_server_
  // get_* / latin_autocomplete_get_* / latin_deadkey_get_* precedent).

  pub let indic_inscript_get_provider_id : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read provider_kind_id from cell[+0][31:0]. Zero-extension via shl+shr. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gpi_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let indic_inscript_get_session_id : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read session_kind_id from cell[+0][63:32]. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gsi_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 0];
        shr rax, 32;
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let indic_inscript_get_keymap_ptr : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read keymap_ptr from cell[+8] (full u64). Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gkp_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 8];
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let indic_inscript_get_mode : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read mode from cell[+16][7:0]. u8 extraction via shl 56 / shr 56. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gm_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 16];
        shl rax, 56;
        shr rax, 56;
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let indic_inscript_get_prefix_offset : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read phonetic_prefix_offset from cell[+16][63:32]. u32 zero-extend via shr 32. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gpx_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 16];
        shr rax, 32;
        ret
      }
    }

  pub let indic_inscript_get_pending : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): read pending_output_offset from cell[+24][31:0]. Zero-extension via shl+shr. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_gpo_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 24];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 7 -- INIT FACTORY
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_init(engine_ptr, process_kind_id, mode, keymap_ptr)
  //   -> u64
  //
  //   Populate a caller-owned 32-byte engine cell AND register this
  //   engine with the KIND_IME_PROVIDER substrate as a LANG_INDIC_HI
  //   provider. Contract:
  //
  //     (1) engine_ptr == 0                     -> IIS_ENGINE_NULL
  //     (2) process_kind_id == 0                -> IIS_PROCESS_NULL
  //     (3) mode > IIS_MODE_MAX                 -> IIS_BAD_MODE
  //     (4) keymap_ptr == 0                     -> IIS_KEYMAP_NULL
  //     (5) engine already initialized (cell[+0][31:0] != 0)
  //                                             -> IIS_ALREADY_INIT
  //     (6) call ime_provider_register(process_kind_id, IIS_LANG_
  //         INDIC_HI, IIS_LOCALE_UNLOCALED, IIS_CAPS_DEFAULT); on
  //         refusal sentinel (upper 32 bits non-zero, i.e. any
  //         0xFFFFE9A* IMP_* code) return       -> IIS_REGISTER_REFUSED
  //     (7) success: stamp the cell:
  //           cell[+0]   = provider_kind_id[31:0] | 0 (session not bound)
  //           cell[+8]   = keymap_ptr (full u64)
  //           cell[+16]  = mode[7:0]  (prefix_offset=0, reserved=0)
  //           cell[+24]  = 0 (no pending output; reserved=0)
  //         bump IIS_ST_INITS; return IIS_OK.
  //
  //   Refusal funnel bumps IIS_ST_REFUSED once at
  //   indic_inscript_init_refused.
  //
  //   Note the arg-order the prompt names is (provider, mode,
  //   keymap_ptr); mirroring latin_deadkey_init's schema, engine_ptr
  //   is prepended so the caller's cell is the first arg (rdi), and
  //   process_kind_id follows in rsi (matching the router-side
  //   convention that "which process owns this?" is always the
  //   second cap arg). Full order: (engine_ptr, process_kind_id,
  //   mode, keymap_ptr) -- SysV rdi/rsi/rdx/rcx.
  //
  //   Register plan (four callee-save pushes + sub rsp,8 = 40 bytes;
  //   entry rsp%16==8 -> 40+8=48 %16==0 for nested calls
  //   (ime_provider_register + indic_inscript_note)):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr
  //     r12 = process_kind_id
  //     r13 = mode
  //     r14 = keymap_ptr (moved to r14 to free rcx across the
  //           ime_provider_register call which takes rcx as caps)
  //     r15 = provider_kind_id (from ime_provider_register)
  pub let inscript_init : (u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) (process_kind_id: u64) (mode: u64) (keymap_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): register + engine-cell init factory. Five callee-save pushes = 40 bytes; entry rsp%16==8 -> after five pushes rsp%16 == (8-40) mod 16 == 0, aligned for nested calls (ime_provider_register + indic_inscript_note). No padding sub needed (odd-push-count keeps SysV alignment on its own). Args stashed BEFORE any nested call: rbx=engine_ptr, r12=process_kind_id, r13=mode, r14=keymap_ptr, r15 receives provider_kind_id. Refusal-sentinel detection on ime_provider_register uses shr r10,32 / cmp r10,0 (mirrors latin_autocomplete_init / latin_deadkey_init). Cell stamp writes four u64 words directly with `mov [rbx+off], rN` (encoder-conservative). No `test`, no `add reg,[mem]`, no MOVABS. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_init_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;
        push r14;
        push r15;

        mov rbx, rdi;                       // engine_ptr
        mov r12, rsi;                       // process_kind_id
        mov r13, rdx;                       // mode
        mov r14, rcx;                       // keymap_ptr

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_init_null_engine;

        // (2) process_kind_id null
        cmp r12, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_init_null_process;

        // (3) mode validity
        cmp r13, 1;
        ja  indic_inscript_init_bad_mode;

        // (4) keymap_ptr null
        cmp r14, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_init_null_keymap;

        // (5) already-init check: cell[+0][31:0] (provider_kind_id) != 0
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        jne indic_inscript_init_already;

        // (6) register with ProviderKind substrate as LANG_INDIC_HI.
        //     ime_provider_register(process, lang, locale, caps)
        //       rdi = process_kind_id
        //       rsi = IIS_LANG_INDIC_HI (4)
        //       rdx = IIS_LOCALE_UNLOCALED (0)
        //       rcx = IIS_CAPS_DEFAULT (0x05)
        mov rdi, r12;
        mov rsi, 4;                         // IIS_LANG_INDIC_HI
        xor rdx, rdx;                       // IIS_LOCALE_UNLOCALED = 0
        mov rcx, 0x05;                      // IIS_CAPS_DEFAULT
        call ime_provider_register;

        // Refusal detection: IMP_* sentinels are 0xFFFFE9A0..AF, upper
        // 32 bits non-zero. A legal row_id is 0..7, upper 32 bits zero.
        mov r10, rax;
        shr r10, 32;
        cmp r10, 0;
        jne indic_inscript_init_reg_refused;

        mov r15, rax;                       // r15 = provider_kind_id

        // (7) stamp the cell.

        // cell[+0]: provider_kind_id[31:0] | session_kind_id[63:32]=0
        mov rax, r15;
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;                        // rax = provider_id & 0xFFFFFFFF
        mov [rbx + 0], rax;

        // cell[+8]: keymap_ptr (full u64)
        mov [rbx + 8], r14;

        // cell[+16]: mode[7:0] (prefix_offset=0, reserved=0)
        //   pack: mode & 0xFF
        mov rax, r13;
        shl rax, 56;
        shr rax, 56;                        // rax = mode & 0xFF
        mov [rbx + 16], rax;

        // cell[+24]: 0 (no pending output; reserved=0)
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        // Bump IIS_ST_INITS.
        mov rdi, 6;                         // IIS_ST_INITS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        xor rax, rax;                       // IIS_OK
        jmp indic_inscript_init_out;

      indic_inscript_init_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_init_refused;
      indic_inscript_init_null_process:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FE;                // IIS_PROCESS_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_init_refused;
      indic_inscript_init_bad_mode:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FC;                // IIS_BAD_MODE
        jmp indic_inscript_init_refused;
      indic_inscript_init_null_keymap:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FD;                // IIS_KEYMAP_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_init_refused;
      indic_inscript_init_already:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FB;                // IIS_ALREADY_INIT
        jmp indic_inscript_init_refused;
      indic_inscript_init_reg_refused:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7F9;                // IIS_REGISTER_REFUSED
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_init_refused:
        // Stash refusal code across the note call.
        mov r15, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, r15;

      indic_inscript_init_out:
        pop r15;
        pop r14;
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 8 -- PHONETIC RESOLVE (STUB)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_resolve(engine_ptr) -> resolved_output_offset | IIS_*
  //
  //   Trigger the phonetic-transliteration resolver on the currently
  //   accumulated Roman prefix. On hit, sets cell[+24][31:0] to the
  //   interned offset of the resolved Devanagari string and returns
  //   that offset; on miss, returns 0 (no output; the accumulated
  //   prefix is discarded either way per the "commit-or-drop" contract
  //   of the resolver -- the user can retype if they want a
  //   different transliteration).
  //
  //   Body is CURRENTLY a stub: bumps IIS_ST_RESOLVES, clears the
  //   phonetic prefix (cell[+16][63:32] <- 0), and returns 0. The
  //   real resolver lands with the satellite-side substrate that
  //   wires the transliteration dictionary (a trie or FST over
  //   Roman syllable strings with Devanagari code-point-sequence
  //   leaves, out of scope for this row). The state machine's
  //   correctness does not depend on the resolver body: a stubbed
  //   resolver makes every phonetic word return no output, which is
  //   one of the two legitimate outcomes the state machine handles.
  //   Once the real resolver lands, hits populate pending_output_
  //   offset instead.
  //
  //   Register plan (one callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8
  //   -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr (kept live for the cell-clear op)
  pub let inscript_resolve : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): phonetic-transliteration resolver (currently a stub that returns 0; real resolver deferred to satellite substrate). One callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8 -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call. Order: null / init gates, clear the phonetic prefix field, bump IIS_ST_RESOLVES, return 0. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_rv_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;

        mov rbx, rdi;

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_rv_null_engine;

        // (2) init check
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_rv_not_init;

        // Stub: clear cell[+16][63:32] (the phonetic prefix).
        // Preserve cell[+16][31:0] (mode + reserved) via
        // shl 32 / shr 32.
        mov rax, [rbx + 16];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;                        // rax = mode|reserved with prefix=0
        mov [rbx + 16], rax;

        // Bump IIS_ST_RESOLVES.
        mov rdi, 3;                         // IIS_ST_RESOLVES
        call indic_inscript_note;

        xor rax, rax;                       // miss (no output)
        jmp indic_inscript_rv_out;

      indic_inscript_rv_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_rv_refused;
      indic_inscript_rv_not_init:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FA;                // IIS_NOT_INIT
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_rv_refused:
        mov rbx, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, rbx;

      indic_inscript_rv_out:
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 9 -- ON-KEY DISPATCH
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_on_key(engine_ptr, keycode) -> u64
  //
  //   Dispatch a single key event through the mode-appropriate arm.
  //
  //     MODE_INSCRIPT: direct table lookup. Probe keymap[keycode]
  //                    (u16 array indexed by the low 7 bits of the
  //                    keycode). A nonzero codepoint commits (return
  //                    IIS_TAG_COMMITTED with the codepoint in
  //                    bits [23:8]); zero returns IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH
  //                    (unmapped slot; caller passes the key through
  //                    to the raw text stream).
  //
  //     MODE_PHONETIC: accumulator. Space or Enter fires the
  //                    resolver on the accumulated prefix and returns
  //                    IIS_TAG_RESOLVED (the caller reads pending_
  //                    output_offset via inscript_get_pending or
  //                    invokes inscript_commit to dispatch). ESC
  //                    fires the reset (return IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH;
  //                    the ESC itself is swallowed). Any other key
  //                    is appended to the prefix (the append itself
  //                    is deferred to the future interned-string
  //                    substrate; today the body only bumps IIS_ST_
  //                    ACCUMULATES) and returns IIS_TAG_PENDING.
  //
  //   Returns (per §1.5 return encoding):
  //     IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH   (0)  low byte
  //     IIS_TAG_PENDING       (1)  low byte
  //     IIS_TAG_COMMITTED     (2)  low byte + u16 codepoint in [23:8]
  //     IIS_TAG_RESOLVED      (3)  low byte (caller reads pending_
  //                                output_offset)
  //
  //   Refusal sentinels (upper 32 bits set):
  //     IIS_ENGINE_NULL / IIS_NOT_INIT / IIS_BAD_KEYCODE / IIS_BAD_STATE
  //
  //   Register plan (three callee-save pushes = 24 bytes; entry
  //   rsp%16==8 -> after three pushes rsp%16 == (8-24) mod 16 == 0,
  //   aligned for nested calls (indic_inscript_keycode_valid,
  //   indic_inscript_note, inscript_resolve). No padding sub needed
  //   (odd-push-count keeps SysV alignment on its own):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr
  //     r12 = keycode
  //     r13 = mode (loaded from cell[+16][7:0] after init gate)
  pub let inscript_on_key : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) (keycode: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): state-machine entry point. Three callee-save pushes = 24 bytes; entry rsp%16==8 -> (8-24) mod 16 == 0, aligned for nested calls (indic_inscript_keycode_valid + indic_inscript_note + inscript_resolve). Order: (1) null gate. (2) init gate. (3) keycode range gate (< IIS_KEYMAP_SIZE). (4) load mode from cell[+16][7:0]. (5) branch on mode. MODE_INSCRIPT: probe keymap[keycode], commit or passthrough. MODE_PHONETIC: check keycode vs SPACE/ENTER (resolve), ESC (reset), else accumulate. (6) bump the mode-appropriate stats counter. (7) return packed status word per §1.5. r12 keeps keycode live across nested calls; r13 keeps mode. No `test`, no `add reg,[mem]`, no MOVABS, no `mov_wzx`. Small immediates only. u16 keymap-entry load uses `mov ax, [ptr + rcx*2]` then shl 48 / shr 48 zero-extend. Wait -- `mov ax, [...]` is a 16-bit load that leaves upper bits UNMODIFIED; encoder-conservative approach uses `mov rax, [ptr + rcx*2]` (64-bit load) then shl 48 / shr 48. That's what we do. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_ok_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        push r13;

        mov rbx, rdi;
        mov r12, rsi;

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_null_engine;

        // (2) init check
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_not_init;

        // (3) keycode validity (must fit in 7 bits: < IIS_KEYMAP_SIZE=128)
        mov rdi, r12;
        call indic_inscript_keycode_valid;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_bad_key;

        // (4) load mode from cell[+16][7:0]
        mov rax, [rbx + 16];
        shl rax, 56;
        shr rax, 56;                        // rax = mode

        // (5) validate mode (defence-in-depth against a corrupt cell)
        cmp rax, 1;
        ja  indic_inscript_ok_bad_state;

        mov r13, rax;                       // r13 = mode

        // (6) key-event stats bump (all paths). This happens BEFORE
        //     the branch so success accounting is uniform.
        mov rdi, 0;                         // IIS_ST_KEY_EVENTS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        // (7) mode dispatch
        cmp r13, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_inscript_path;
        // r13 == 1 (MODE_PHONETIC) falls through
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_path;

        // ==============================================================
        // MODE_INSCRIPT: direct keymap[keycode] lookup
        // ==============================================================
      indic_inscript_ok_inscript_path:
        // Load keymap_ptr from cell[+8].
        mov rax, [rbx + 8];                 // rax = keymap_ptr

        // Compute keymap[keycode]. Each entry is u16, so effective
        // address is keymap_ptr + keycode*2. Encoder-conservative
        // 64-bit load followed by shl 48 / shr 48 to isolate the
        // low u16 (no mov_wzx).
        mov rcx, r12;                       // rcx = keycode
        mov rax, [rax + rcx * 2];           // 64-bit load; upper bits
                                            // are content of adjacent
                                            // keymap slots but we mask
        shl rax, 48;
        shr rax, 48;                        // rax = keymap[keycode] u16

        // If codepoint == 0 -> IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH (unmapped slot).
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_inscript_passthrough;

        // Commit: pack rax into bits [23:8] and OR IIS_TAG_COMMITTED
        // into bits [7:0].
        shl rax, 8;                         // codepoint << 8
        or  rax, 2;                         // | IIS_TAG_COMMITTED
        mov r13, rax;                       // stash across note call

        mov rdi, 1;                         // IIS_ST_COMMITS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        mov rax, r13;                       // restore packed return
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_out;

      indic_inscript_ok_inscript_passthrough:
        xor rax, rax;                       // IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH (0)
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_out;

        // ==============================================================
        // MODE_PHONETIC: accumulator with SPACE/ENTER/ESC triggers
        // ==============================================================
      indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_path:
        // Check ESC (0x1B) -> reset in place, return PASSTHROUGH
        // (the ESC itself is swallowed by the engine).
        cmp r12, 0x1B;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_esc;

        // Check SPACE (0x20) or ENTER (0x0D) -> fire resolver.
        cmp r12, 0x20;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_resolve;
        cmp r12, 0x0D;
        je  indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_resolve;

        // Otherwise: accumulate. The actual prefix-append is
        // deferred to the future interned-string substrate; today
        // the body only bumps IIS_ST_ACCUMULATES to record the
        // event. cell[+16][63:32] stays whatever it was (0 at first
        // key of a fresh round; the substrate will bump the offset
        // once the prefix pool exists).
        mov rdi, 2;                         // IIS_ST_ACCUMULATES
        call indic_inscript_note;

        mov rax, 1;                         // IIS_TAG_PENDING
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_out;

      indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_esc:
        // Clear cell[+16][63:32] (phonetic prefix) preserving
        // cell[+16][31:0] (mode + reserved).
        mov rax, [rbx + 16];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        mov [rbx + 16], rax;

        // Clear cell[+24] (pending output, reserved).
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        mov rdi, 4;                         // IIS_ST_RESETS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        xor rax, rax;                       // IIS_TAG_PASSTHROUGH
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_out;

      indic_inscript_ok_phonetic_resolve:
        // Invoke the resolver. It clears the phonetic prefix as a
        // side effect and returns the resolved output offset (0 =
        // miss). We stash the result into cell[+24][31:0] as
        // pending_output_offset for later inscript_commit dispatch.
        mov rdi, rbx;                       // engine_ptr
        call inscript_resolve;

        // Rewrite cell[+24]: pending_output_offset = rax; reserved
        // stays 0. Encoder-conservative full-word write.
        //   packed = rax & 0xFFFFFFFF (upper 32 bits already 0 on
        //   both hit and miss because the resolver never returns
        //   a full-u32 that exceeds interned-pool size in practice,
        //   but we mask defensively anyway).
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        mov rax, 3;                         // IIS_TAG_RESOLVED
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_out;

      indic_inscript_ok_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_refused;
      indic_inscript_ok_not_init:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FA;                // IIS_NOT_INIT
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_refused;
      indic_inscript_ok_bad_key:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7F8;                // IIS_BAD_KEYCODE
        jmp indic_inscript_ok_refused;
      indic_inscript_ok_bad_state:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7F7;                // IIS_BAD_STATE
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_ok_refused:
        mov r13, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, r13;

      indic_inscript_ok_out:
        pop r13;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 10 -- COMMIT
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_commit(engine_ptr) -> committed_text_offset | IIS_*
  //
  //   Dispatch the pending_output_offset to the caller (the
  //   satellite process's session-side commit path calls
  //   ime_session_commit_text on the bound session with the returned
  //   offset). Clears pending_output_offset as a side effect (the
  //   composition round is over; a subsequent commit against the
  //   same engine returns IIS_NO_PENDING until on_key resolves a
  //   fresh round).
  //
  //   Contract:
  //     (1) engine_ptr == 0            -> IIS_ENGINE_NULL
  //     (2) provider_kind_id == 0      -> IIS_NOT_INIT
  //     (3) pending_output_offset == 0 -> IIS_NO_PENDING
  //     (4) success: read pending_output_offset from cell[+24][31:0];
  //         clear cell[+24] (offset + reserved both zero); bump
  //         IIS_ST_COMMITS; return the offset.
  //
  //   InScript MODE_INSCRIPT commits go DIRECTLY through on_key's
  //   IIS_TAG_COMMITTED return path (single codepoint on the wire,
  //   no need to consult the interned-pool); this commit primitive
  //   is exclusively for MODE_PHONETIC resolved-output dispatch.
  //
  //   Register plan (two callee-save pushes + sub rsp,8 = 24; entry
  //   rsp%16==8 -> 24+8=32 %16==0):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr
  //     r12 = pending offset (stashed across note call)
  pub let inscript_commit : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): commit the pending phonetic output; clear pending. Two callee-save pushes + sub rsp,8 = 24; entry rsp%16==8 -> 32 %16==0 for the note call. Order: null / init / pending gates, then read pending_output_offset, clear cell[+24], bump IIS_ST_COMMITS, return offset. r12 stashes the offset across the note call. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_cm_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;
        push r12;
        sub rsp, 8;

        mov rbx, rdi;

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_cm_null_engine;

        // (2) init check
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_cm_not_init;

        // Load pending_output_offset from cell[+24][31:0]
        mov rax, [rbx + 24];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;                        // rax = pending offset

        // (3) empty-pending check
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_cm_no_pending;

        mov r12, rax;                       // stash offset

        // Clear cell[+24]
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        // Bump IIS_ST_COMMITS
        mov rdi, 1;                         // IIS_ST_COMMITS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        mov rax, r12;                       // committed_text_offset
        jmp indic_inscript_cm_out;

      indic_inscript_cm_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_cm_refused;
      indic_inscript_cm_not_init:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FA;                // IIS_NOT_INIT
        jmp indic_inscript_cm_refused;
      indic_inscript_cm_no_pending:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7F6;                // IIS_NO_PENDING
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_cm_refused:
        mov r12, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, r12;

      indic_inscript_cm_out:
        add rsp, 8;
        pop r12;
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 11 -- SWITCH MODE
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_switch_mode(engine_ptr, new_mode) -> u64
  //
  //   Toggle between MODE_INSCRIPT and MODE_PHONETIC. Any in-flight
  //   phonetic prefix is discarded (the semantic is "the user
  //   changed their mind about typing method mid-word; drop the
  //   half-typed word"). Provider registration is UNCHANGED (the
  //   provider row's caps bitmap already covers both modes; a
  //   re-register would bump the router-side registered_seq and
  //   shuffle the router's most-recent-wins ordering, which is not
  //   what the user asked for).
  //
  //   Contract:
  //     (1) engine_ptr == 0            -> IIS_ENGINE_NULL
  //     (2) provider_kind_id == 0      -> IIS_NOT_INIT
  //     (3) new_mode > IIS_MODE_MAX    -> IIS_BAD_MODE
  //     (4) success: rewrite cell[+16] with mode=new_mode, prefix=0,
  //         reserved=0; clear cell[+24] (drop any pending output
  //         from the outgoing mode); bump IIS_ST_MODE_SWITCHES;
  //         return IIS_OK.
  //
  //   Register plan (one callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8
  //   -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr
  //     r10 = new_mode (scratch across the cell writes; note call
  //           does not clobber r10 across itself but we stash into
  //           rbx-save if needed)
  //
  //   Note: rsi carries new_mode on entry; we move it into r10
  //   before the cell writes so nested calls don't collide.
  pub let inscript_switch_mode : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) (new_mode: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): toggle mode; drop any in-flight phonetic prefix. One callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8 -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call. Order: null / init / mode gates, rewrite cell[+16] with mode=new_mode|prefix=0, clear cell[+24], bump IIS_ST_MODE_SWITCHES, return IIS_OK. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_sm_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;

        mov rbx, rdi;

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_sm_null_engine;

        // (2) init check
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_sm_not_init;

        // (3) mode validity (mode <= 1)
        cmp rsi, 1;
        ja  indic_inscript_sm_bad_mode;

        // (4) rewrite cell[+16]: mode=new_mode, prefix=0, reserved=0.
        mov rax, rsi;
        shl rax, 56;
        shr rax, 56;                        // rax = new_mode & 0xFF
        mov [rbx + 16], rax;

        // Clear cell[+24] (drop any pending output).
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        // Bump IIS_ST_MODE_SWITCHES.
        mov rdi, 5;                         // IIS_ST_MODE_SWITCHES
        call indic_inscript_note;

        xor rax, rax;                       // IIS_OK
        jmp indic_inscript_sm_out;

      indic_inscript_sm_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_sm_refused;
      indic_inscript_sm_not_init:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FA;                // IIS_NOT_INIT
        jmp indic_inscript_sm_refused;
      indic_inscript_sm_bad_mode:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FC;                // IIS_BAD_MODE
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_sm_refused:
        // Stash refusal code via rbx (no longer needed as engine_ptr
        // on the refusal exit); rax carries the code across the
        // note call.
        mov rbx, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, rbx;

      indic_inscript_sm_out:
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 12 -- RESET
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // inscript_reset(engine_ptr) -> u64
  //
  //   Clear all in-flight state: phonetic prefix, pending output.
  //   Mode is NOT touched (a reset is a "cancel the current word"
  //   op, not a "switch typing methods" op). Provider registration
  //   is UNCHANGED.
  //
  //   Contract:
  //     (1) engine_ptr == 0            -> IIS_ENGINE_NULL
  //     (2) provider_kind_id == 0      -> IIS_NOT_INIT
  //     (3) success: clear cell[+16][63:32] (prefix) preserving
  //         cell[+16][31:0] (mode + reserved); clear cell[+24]
  //         (pending + reserved); bump IIS_ST_RESETS; return IIS_OK.
  //
  //   A reset on an empty composition (no prefix, no pending) is
  //   still counted -- an explicit reset with nothing to clear is
  //   a legitimate no-op the caller may issue, and the telemetry
  //   records it faithfully.
  //
  //   Register plan (one callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8
  //   -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call):
  //     rbx = engine_ptr
  pub let inscript_reset : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (engine_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G11-M4-006 (paideia-os #2322): clear phonetic prefix + pending output; leave mode intact. One callee-save push = 8 bytes; entry rsp%16==8 -> after push rsp%16==0 for the note call. Order: null / init gates, clear cell[+16][63:32] (preserving mode+reserved via shl 32 / shr 32), clear cell[+24], bump IIS_ST_RESETS, return IIS_OK. Labels prefixed indic_inscript_rs_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;

        mov rbx, rdi;

        // (1) engine_ptr null
        cmp rbx, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_rs_null_engine;

        // (2) init check
        mov rax, [rbx + 0];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  indic_inscript_rs_not_init;

        // Clear phonetic prefix; preserve mode + reserved.
        mov rax, [rbx + 16];
        shl rax, 32;
        shr rax, 32;
        mov [rbx + 16], rax;

        // Clear pending output.
        xor rax, rax;
        mov [rbx + 24], rax;

        // Bump IIS_ST_RESETS.
        mov rdi, 4;                         // IIS_ST_RESETS
        call indic_inscript_note;

        xor rax, rax;                       // IIS_OK
        jmp indic_inscript_rs_out;

      indic_inscript_rs_null_engine:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FF;                // IIS_ENGINE_NULL
        jmp indic_inscript_rs_refused;
      indic_inscript_rs_not_init:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFE7FA;                // IIS_NOT_INIT
        // fallthrough

      indic_inscript_rs_refused:
        mov rbx, rax;
        mov rdi, 7;                         // IIS_ST_REFUSED
        call indic_inscript_note;
        mov rax, rbx;

      indic_inscript_rs_out:
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }
}
